-- AI product photos, the Shopify Sidekick way (owner's decision, 2026-10-18):
-- the photo editor's Scene option re-shoots the merchant's real photo in a
-- setting they pick or describe, instead of placing a cut-out on a drawn set,
-- and Mink AI chat can put a product in any scene or on a model and keep
-- changing it in the same conversation. 5 Mink credits per photo in both.
-- Two guides edited in place, sentence by sentence; no new section.

UPDATE public.help_articles SET body=replace(body, $old$A catalogue product photo is different: ask for one and Mink makes a clean studio shot from a real photo of the item (the product's existing photo or one you attach), never from a description alone, and proposes it as the product's photo for your approval.$old$, $new$A product photo is different: Mink makes it from a real photo of the item (the product's existing photo or one you attach), never from a description alone. Ask for a clean studio shot, or describe a scene, for example "show this coat hanging from a tree in a garden", then keep asking for changes in the same conversation, such as "now a close-up on a model standing in a forest". Under each product photo, select <strong>Use as product photo</strong> to have Mink propose it as the product's photo for your approval, or <strong>Try again</strong> for another version. Each product photo uses 5 Mink credits. Mink redraws the product in the scene, so compare it with the real item before you use it: small details such as a print or a label can change. A model in a photo is always an adult and never a real or famous person.$new$), updated_at=now() WHERE slug='use-mink-ai-in-your-dashboard' AND status='published';

UPDATE public.help_articles SET body=replace(body, $old$or ask Mink for a new catalogue photo of a product that already has one.$old$, $new$or ask Mink for a new photo of a product that already has one, in a studio or in a scene you describe.$new$), updated_at=now() WHERE slug='use-mink-ai-in-your-dashboard' AND status='published';

UPDATE public.help_articles SET body=replace(body, $old$In the Mink AI chat you can also ask for a new catalogue photo of a product: Mink makes it from the product's existing photo, keeps it under Media and proposes it as the product's photo for your approval (3 Mink credits for the picture and 1 for the photo change).$old$, $new$In the Mink AI chat you can also ask for a new photo of a product, in a studio or in a scene you describe: Mink makes it from the product's existing photo, keeps it under Media and proposes it as the product's photo for your approval (5 Mink credits for the picture and 1 for the photo change).$new$), updated_at=now() WHERE slug='add-product-images-and-variants' AND status='published';

UPDATE public.help_articles SET body=replace(body, $old$to put your product on white, a colour, a transparent background or a scene such as a marble counter or linen. Your product$old$, $new$to put your product on white, a colour or a transparent background. Your product$new$), updated_at=now() WHERE slug='add-product-images-and-variants' AND status='published';

UPDATE public.help_articles SET body=replace(body, $old$Choose <strong>Scene</strong> to place the product in one of eight scenes: Mink AI draws only the empty scene, never your product. A new scene uses 5 Mink credits and is saved, so placing your other products in it is free and your photos match. Select <strong>Draw a new one</strong> to replace a saved scene.$old$, $new$To show the product in a setting instead, select <strong>Put in a scene</strong>: choose a scene such as a marble counter or a garden, or describe your own, for example hanging from a tree branch or worn by a model on a city street, then select <strong>Create photo</strong>. Mink AI photographs your product in the scene, so it redraws the product too: compare it with your real product before you choose <strong>Use this photo</strong>, because small details such as a print or a label can change. Each scene photo uses 5 Mink credits, <strong>Try again</strong> makes another, and every photo you make stays on screen to choose from.$new$), updated_at=now() WHERE slug='add-product-images-and-variants' AND status='published';
